<neuroml xmlns="http://www.neuroml.org/schema/neuroml2"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.neuroml.org/schema/neuroml2 https://raw.github.com/NeuroML/NeuroML2/master/Schemas/NeuroML2/NeuroML_v2.3.xsd"
         id="IzhikevichNetworkExitModel">

  <!--
    Phase-2 exit model #1 (ticket #67 [H2], arch §5 Phase 2): an izhikevich
    network - two `izhikevich2007Cell` neurons (a REAL vendored NeuroML
    ComponentType, third_party/neuroml2/std_lib/Cells.xml, not a custom
    inline declaration like the GLIF fixtures) wired via a real
    `alphaCurrentSynapse` connection, "DrivenPop" directly stimulated by a
    pulseGenerator current step, "TargetPop" receiving only the propagated
    connection. Same RS (Regular Spiking) parameter set
    tests/nonlinear_cell_lowering_tests.cpp's own
    izhikevich2007Cell_regular_spiking_pattern_under_current_step acceptance
    test already verified reproduces Izhikevich's own textbook Regular
    Spiking pattern - this fixture additionally drives it through the real
    jLEMS reference (that prior ticket never did) and puts it in a genuine
    (if minimal) network, per this ticket's own "more than one cell with
    real connectivity, doesn't need to be elaborate" scope note.

    izhikevich2007Cell is real vendored NeuroML, so unlike GLIF3Cell/
    GLIF1Cell this file needs no inline <ComponentType> declaration -
    spikecorec's own front-end auto-merges every file under its standard
    library directory at parse time regardless of <include> (NML_Parser::
    load_standard_library, src/nml/nml.cpp), and jNeuroML/jLEMS gets the
    same real ComponentType via LEMS_izhikevich_network.xml's own
    <Include file="Cells.xml"/> (which transitively includes Synapses.xml,
    see that file's own header comment for why).

    Populations are declared `type="populationList"` with explicit
    `<instance>` children and stimulus/connectivity wired via `<inputList>`/
    `<connectionWD>` - the SAME real, jLEMS-proven-working shape
    glif_ei_network.nml's own header comment documents (this exact jLEMS
    build, bundled with pyneuroml 1.3.22, has documented trouble resolving
    indexed per-member access against a plain population/`explicitInput` in
    some shapes; populationList+inputList+connection is the one already
    proven to work end to end for a real multi-population network in this
    tree). `connectionWD` (not the plain, attribute-free `connection`) is
    used so an explicit `weight` can be set (`delay` is required alongside
    it by the schema - ConnectionWD - so this fixture sets it to "0ms",
    i.e. no meaningful delay here; the delayed-coupling exit model
    (delayed_coupling_network.nml) is what exercises a real, non-trivial
    delay value).

    Regular Spiking under this pulseGenerator step is a genuine, exact
    (within tolerance) comparison target for DrivenPop, mirroring ticket
    #61's own GLIF3 single-cell precedent - but per this file's own
    header comment (and exit_model_validation_tests.cpp's documented
    known limitation #3, carried over unchanged from ticket #61): a
    downstream neuron's real per-edge synapse dynamics are not yet invoked
    by AssembledModel's fixed propagate stage (only a shared-basis/
    constant-weight k^2-tree scatter is), so TargetPop's own trajectory in
    spikecorec is NOT expected to match its real jLEMS reference-driven
    trajectory - captured here anyway (real data, not fabricated), but the
    DISABLED_ comparison test only asserts DrivenPop's own exact match.
  -->
  <izhikevich2007Cell id="izhRsCellInstance" v0="-60mV" C="100pF" k="0.7nS_per_mV"
                      vr="-60mV" vt="-40mV" vpeak="35mV" a="0.03per_ms" b="-2nS" c="-50mV" d="100pA"/>

  <!-- alphaCurrentSynapse's own "weight" Property is left at its defaultValue (1) here - this
       exact jLEMS build ignores a plain XML attribute override of a Property with a defaultValue
       (warns "Unused attribute ... weight" at simulation time, silently keeping the default
       instead), so setting one explicitly here would be misleading; the connectionWD element
       below carries the ACTUAL per-edge weight spikecorec's own front-end reads
       (ConnectionEntry::weight, model_specification.cpp's own numeric_attribute_or on the
       <connectionWD> element itself, a structurally different attribute from this Property). -->
  <alphaCurrentSynapse id="izhCurrSynapse" tau="2ms" ibase="1nA"/>

  <pulseGenerator id="pulseGen1" delay="10ms" duration="200ms" amplitude="150pA"/>

  <network id="IzhikevichNet">
    <population id="DrivenPop" component="izhRsCellInstance" type="populationList" size="1">
      <instance id="0"><location x="0" y="0" z="0"/></instance>
    </population>
    <population id="TargetPop" component="izhRsCellInstance" type="populationList" size="1">
      <instance id="0"><location x="1" y="0" z="0"/></instance>
    </population>
    <inputList id="stimList" component="pulseGen1" population="DrivenPop">
      <input id="0" target="../DrivenPop/0/izhRsCellInstance" destination="synapses"/>
    </inputList>
    <projection id="DrivenToTarget" presynapticPopulation="DrivenPop" postsynapticPopulation="TargetPop" synapse="izhCurrSynapse">
      <connectionWD id="0" preCellId="../DrivenPop/0/izhRsCellInstance" postCellId="../TargetPop/0/izhRsCellInstance" weight="1" delay="0ms"/>
    </projection>
  </network>

  <Simulation id="sim1" length="230ms" step="0.1ms" target="IzhikevichNet">
    <OutputFile id="membraneTrace" fileName="izhikevich_network_membrane_trace.dat">
      <OutputColumn id="v_driven" quantity="DrivenPop/0/izhRsCellInstance/v"/>
      <OutputColumn id="u_driven" quantity="DrivenPop/0/izhRsCellInstance/u"/>
      <OutputColumn id="v_target" quantity="TargetPop/0/izhRsCellInstance/v"/>
    </OutputFile>
    <EventOutputFile id="spikesFile" fileName="izhikevich_network_spikes.dat" format="TIME_ID">
      <EventSelection id="sel_driven" select="DrivenPop/0/izhRsCellInstance" eventPort="spike"/>
      <EventSelection id="sel_target" select="TargetPop/0/izhRsCellInstance" eventPort="spike"/>
    </EventOutputFile>
  </Simulation>
</neuroml>
